**Analysis:**

"EQ Power" was the branding Mercedes-Benz previously used for its Plug-in Hybrid Electric Vehicles (PHEVs). While this specific branding has been largely phased out for the newest models (often replaced by a simple 'e' suffix like S 580 e), the user's intent is clearly to evaluate the Plug-in Hybrid version of the latest S-Class.

The primary PHEV model in the current W223 S-Class lineup is the **Mercedes-Benz S 580 e** (available in RWD or 4MATIC depending on the market). This model combines a 3.0L Inline-6 engine with a significant electric motor and battery pack, offering substantial electric-only range and DC fast charging capability.

